  "question": {
    "text": "<p>In the given potentiometer circuit arrangement, the balancing length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AC</mi></math> is measured to be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>250</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. When the galvanometer connection is shifted from point (1) to point (2) in the given diagram, the balancing length becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math>. The ratio of the emf of two cells&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></math> is:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0203_300de84084ed.png\" style=\"width: 285px; height: 209px;\" /></p>"
  },
